@title Justify Implement/Update Actions
@sigils [🎴/功]
@audience fulab agents, musn server
@tone technical
@style pattern
@why no problem-corpus source matched (@holds-at absent; holds-token and id-text searches over every node in [problems] found no match). Negative claim per the committed check futon2 holes labs library-loop runs l6_no_source_check.py, receipt runs/L10-no-source-check.edn. Rationale not invented (L10 rationale-backfill, zai-1, 2026-09-05)
@how own mechanism: Implement/update actions must include a justification tied to the pattern. (source: this pattern's ! conclusion line; L10 rationale-backfill, zai-1, 2026-09-05)

! conclusion: Implement/update actions must include a justification tied to the pattern.

  + context: Pattern-driven edits need explicit rationale to be auditable.

  + IF:
    Implement/update notes omit why the edit follows the pattern.

  + HOWEVER:
    Short notes are preferred to reduce overhead.

  + THEN:
    Require implement/update notes to state why the edit follows the pattern.

  + BECAUSE:
    Justified notes prevent unreasoned edits and make warnings meaningful.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    - evidence: pattern-action implement/update notes include a rationale clause.
    - evidence-shape: {:action :string, :note :string, :pattern/id :string}
